-- why primary and foreign keys matter?
-- in a relational database data lives in multiple tables but those tables must be connected somehow
-- we do this using keys
-- primary key(pk) a column or set of columns that uniquely identif a row in a table
-- >student_id, customer_id, product_id
-- foriegn key (fk) a column  inone table that refers to a pk in another table
-- a foreign key is just a pk in another table

-- think of pk/fk as parent child relationship - a parent can have manmy children but each child points to one parent

